title: Define PackageId data structure and interning strategy
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-15T05:51:53'
updated_at: '2026-06-15T05:52:03'
result: 'src/pkgid.rs lands the PackageId model per scope.md §1.1: interned u32 handles
  (PkgId, ScopePath) + side tables (the decided interned-handle design, not crammed
  into intern.rs). PackageRecord{name, owner_scope, version:SemVer, semantic_hash:[u8;32]}.
  ScopePath::intern/child/render gives `foo:baz` dotted display; root = empty. PkgId
  dedups on (name,scope,version) so distinct versions = distinct ids (multi-version
  identity), fully_qualified() renders `foo:baz:bar`, mangle_prefix() = first 4 hash
  bytes hex (scope.md §1.3 `<pkgid_hash>_<module>_<name>`). PkgId::root(name) = single-package
  fast-path identity (2-32-3-3 foundation). 7 unit tests.'
description: Implement PackageId{name, owner_scope, version, semantic_hash} as an
  interned handle backed by a side table (per the 'lean' decision in the task). Define
  construction, equality, and hashing semantics so that distinct versions produce
  distinct non-unifiable identities. Done when the PackageId type, intern table, and
  handle API exist with unit tests covering interning dedup and version-distinct identity.
  Depends on 2-32-1 (Q4 multi-version/coherence decision).
